export const additionsHelp = "\nAdditional commands\n  pullboard tool-build [promote <commit> --gate-receipt <native-full-gate-id>]  show the board's pinned tools or promote a gated build for new commands\n  pullboard cells [--json]             each cell sealed or unsealed at HEAD, and the commit that broke an unsealed one; read-only\n  pullboard compact [--dry-run]       archive job steps of items landed or withdrawn over 30 days ago into a gzip file beside the board, then shrink the board file\n  pullboard contribute check <file> [shape]  print every failure of a contribution record file with its rule, fix and skill command; exits 1 when any\n  pullboard contribute check --issue <N> <shape>  the same check on the body of GitHub issue N\n  pullboard explain <table>            a move table's guards in order, each with its refusal code and next step; read-only\n  pullboard field declare <name> <text|choice|number> [--choices a,b]   declare a typed item field; needs items.typedFields on\n  pullboard field set <id> <name> <value>   set an item's value for a declared field; a wrong type is refused with FIELD_TYPE\n  pullboard flow tune [--window <duration>] [--apply] [--json]  the line controller's cycle clock and its chosen change from two adjacent board windows; read-only, changes no setting; --apply (coordinator, line.tune on, cycle due) records the one change or reverts the last\n  pullboard heartbeat [--claims]      record this seat's local session activity; no board move; --claims keeps beating while the seat holds a claim or queued gate\n  pullboard labels [--json]            each label with its min, max, holders and unmet minimum; read-only\n  pullboard link <child> [--by <principal>] [--key <file>]  sign one states link between this board and a child board on this machine; both boards' signers approve\n  pullboard maintenance [--json]      archive and prune idle worktrees when worktreeMaintenance.enabled is true\n  pullboard mutate <cell> [--all] [--item <id>]  seed single-line faults in a throwaway copy of a cell and say which of its own tests catch each; changed lines vs main, --all for every line; --item writes the per-kind score onto that item; report only\n  pullboard red explain <test-file> [--json]  show observed red history, matching source changes, and the failure frame\n  pullboard replay <table> [--days N] [--against <tag>]  how often a move table agrees with the moves the board recorded, with each disagreement's event id; with --against, also how the release tag's table and the current one each fared; read-only\n  pullboard replay --all --against <tag|last> [--days N] [--json] [--fail-on-drift]  judges every current move table against one release (last is the newest vX.Y.Z tag), then says drifted or clean (--fail-on-drift exits 1 on drift); needs moves.judgeByRelease on; read-only\n  pullboard route --suggest           the open strong items whose shape meets the light rule (a check, a brief, at most 3 tagged clauses and 3 files); read-only\n  pullboard rules [--limit <N>] [--json]  replay the whole event log through the lifecycle rules, read-only: the agreement rate, then each disagreement with its event id\n  pullboard search <text>              the top 5 items most like the text, with score, id, state and title; read-only\n  pullboard seats                     current seat states and local 24-hour timing ledger\n  pullboard stats agents [--window <duration>] [--until <ISO time>]  per seat and hour: items claimed, submitted and landed, the most items held at once, and the median and p90 wait from a submit or test start to the seat's next board action\n  pullboard stats disk [--prune] [--dry-run]  disk used under .git/pullboard per store; --prune ages out old raw logs and archives\n  pullboard stats moves [--limit <N>] [--transcripts <file>]  native event moves and separately supplied command transcripts per landed item\n  pullboard stats pipeline [--limit <N>]  recorded stage times and retry/reopen causes for the last N landed items\n  pullboard stats review [--window <duration>] [--until <ISO time>]  review queue depth by hour, time from submit to verdict, and reject rate per reviewer family\n  pullboard stats runners [--window <duration>] [--until <ISO time>]  runner slot wait (queued to running) p50/p90/max and queue depth per job kind and hour\n  pullboard stats runners --health [--window <duration>] [--until <ISO time>]  run time per job kind per runner (p50/p90) and runner up spans, lost leases, retries and re-placed jobs\n  pullboard stats runners --lag [--window <duration>] [--until <ISO time>]  main check lag: time from each main commit landing to its first full-suite result, and to its first red (--main-lag is the same)\n  pullboard stats time                  last claim-to-submit build minutes and criterion size for every landed item\n  pullboard timeline <id> [--json]                    one item's stages with deltas, the bucket summary and its longest gap, read only\n  pullboard timeline --fleet [--since 3h] [--json]    the fleet's stage medians, time shares, gates per landed item and slowest items, read only\n  pullboard trace <agent|item> [--since 2h] [--json]  an agent's or an item's timeline from the command trace and the board's events\n  pullboard update  run the upgrade that matches how Pullboard was installed, then print what changed\n\n";
